#: inc/options/theme-options.php:579
msgid "Off by default. When on, logged-out visitors get a 503 \"back shortly\" page that search engines treat as temporary. Administrators and editors still see the live site, and nothing is deleted or unpublished. Switch it off here to bring the site back."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/agency-layout.php:236
msgid "Off by default. When on, the home page is the agency landing page below: no menu, no ticker, a contact form above the fold and at the bottom. Switch it off to bring the usual home page back."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:568
msgid "Off by default. When on, the login screen uses the site logo, colours and typeface instead of the WordPress default. This changes appearance only: it does not alter how anyone signs in, and it does not add login security. If a login-branding plugin is already active, that plugin keeps control and this setting does nothing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:512
msgid "Offer the site in Bahasa Melayu (/ms/)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:517
msgid "Offer the site in Simplified Chinese (/zh-hans/)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:522
msgid "Offer the site in Traditional Chinese (/zh-hant/)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/agency-layout.php:242
msgid "On by default. About, Team, Services, Case Studies, Insights, Contact, FAQ and every other page redirect to the home page (a temporary 302, so switching the layout off restores them), and they leave the sitemaps and the language versions (the legal pages keep theirs). The ad landing pages, their thank-you pages and the legal pages (privacy, terms) stay reachable. Nothing is deleted. Turn this off to keep the other pages live next to the agency home page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:591
msgid "On by default. Application passwords let a mobile app, a connector plugin or a script log in to the REST API with a separate password. While this is on, WordPress refuses them and hides the section on every user profile, which closes one more way in for anyone who has guessed a login. Switch it off only while an integration you use needs them."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:585
msgid "On by default. PHP notices, warnings and deprecation messages are captured and written to the error log instead of being printed into the page. This matters beyond tidiness: a printed notice is output, and once output has been sent no header can be set for the rest of the request, so a single notice from one plugin cascades into failed redirects and cookies. Administrators see a summary panel; visitors see nothing. Fatal errors are always handled separately and show the branded error page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/agency-layout.php:300
msgid "On by default. SEO links to the SEO audit page, Paid Media to the Google Ads management page and Social Media to the paid social page. The other three services have no landing page yet, so their cards carry no link. A visitor who arrives from this home page is let through; the pages stay closed to every other click from the site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/options/theme-options.php:597
msgid "On by default. Section headings, cards and stats rise gently into place as you scroll, and the hero mark drifts behind the content. Only opacity and transform are animated, so nothing shifts position and page layout is unaffected. Visitors whose device is set to reduce motion never see any of it regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""

